><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIHON YAMAMURA GLASS CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKABAYASHI HAJIMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ZHANG ZUYI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIHON YAMAMURA GLASS CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKABAYASHI, HAJIMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ZHANG, ZUYI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WAKABAYASHI HAJIMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ZHANG ZUYI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WAKABAYASHI, HAJIMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ZHANG, ZUYI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coating composition characterized by comprising: an alcohol dispersion, as component (A), which comprises an alcohol dispersion medium and surface-hydrophobized silica dispersed therein and has a silica content of 80 wt.% or higher based on all solid matters; a solution as component (B) which contains a silicone oligomer obtained by the reaction of an alkoxysilane with water and containing units having an average structure represented by R&lt;1&gt;nSiOx/2(OH) y (OR&lt;2&gt;) z (wherein R&lt;1&gt; is C1-3 alkyl, phenyl, or vinyl; R&lt;2&gt; is C1-3 alkyl; and 0.8&lt;/=n&lt;/=1.7, 2&lt;x&lt;3.2, y&gt;0, z&gt;0, and y+z=4-n-x); and a hardener as component (C). The coating composition has excellent storage stability after addition of the hardener, is less apt to suffer aggregation of fine silica particles in spray coating, and can form a coating film excellent in weatherability, water resistance, chemical resistance, and adhesion and having a high hardness.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de revêtement caractérisée en ce qu'elle renferme: comme composant (A), une dispersion alcoolique comprenant un milieu de dispersion alcoolique et de la silice rendue hydrophobe en surface dispersée dans ledit milieu, la dispersion ayant une teneur en silice supérieure ou égale à 80 % en poids par rapport à l'ensemble des matières solides ; comme composant (B), une solution contenant un oligomère de silicone obtenu par réaction d'un alcoxysilane avec de l'eau et contenant des motifs présentant une structure moyenne représentée par la formule R&lt;1&gt;nSiOx/2(OH)y(OR&lt;2&gt;)z (où R&lt;1&gt; représente alkyle en C1-3, phényle ou vinyle ; R&lt;2&gt; représente alkyle en C1-3; et 0,8 &lt;/=n&lt;/=1,7, 2&lt;x&lt;3,2, y&gt;0, z&gt;0, et y+z=4-n-x; et un agent de durcissement comme composant (C). La composition de revêtement selon l'invention présente une excellente stabilité au stockage après addition de l'agent de durcissement; les fines particules de silice qu'elle contient sont peu susceptibles de s'agglomérer lors de l'application par pulvérisation; et elle peut former un excellent film de revêtement en termes de tenue aux intempéries, de résistance à l'eau, de résistance chimique, d'adhésion et de dureté.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>